WEBVTT

00:00:04.283 --> 00:00:08.185
<i>The family doctor, an icon</i>
<i>of the American experience.</i>

00:00:08.353 --> 00:00:12.153
<i>For generations, they've mended</i>
<i>our wounds and warmed our hearts.</i>

00:00:12.324 --> 00:00:16.886
<i>In my lifetime, Andy Brown was just about</i>
<i>the best example I ever knew of one.</i>

00:00:17.062 --> 00:00:21.055
<i>Doctorwise, that is.</i>
<i>As for the "family" half of the job title...</i>

00:00:21.233 --> 00:00:23.599
<i>... he was a bit rough around the edges.</i>

00:00:23.769 --> 00:00:25.930
Okey-dokey. Here we go.

00:00:26.305 --> 00:00:29.638
- What is that?
- I think it's dinner.

00:00:29.808 --> 00:00:31.241
I found Mom's old recipe book.

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:33.537
- And you cooked it?
- No smart-ass.

00:00:33.712 --> 00:00:36.738
I cooked her meat loaf.
Come on everybody eat up.

00:00:36.915 --> 00:00:39.645
- I think we should say grace.
- You're both half Jewish.

00:00:39.818 --> 00:00:41.979
- Is there a half-Jewish grace?
- Quit stalling.

00:00:42.154 --> 00:00:45.453
Tomorrow we'll try a restaurant
in town okay?

00:00:45.624 --> 00:00:48.718
- lf we're not in the hospital.
- I have my film pick for the night!

00:00:50.495 --> 00:00:53.987
<i>Willy Wonka & the Chocolate Factory.</i>
Excellent choice Delia.

00:00:54.166 --> 00:00:56.100
- Don't let her watch it.
- Be quiet!

00:00:56.268 --> 00:00:57.758
- I miss something?
- Raising her.

00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:00.803
- She can't watch that movie. It upsets her.
- It does not!

00:01:00.973 --> 00:01:03.498
Not if you don't count screams
and sleeping on my floor.

00:01:03.709 --> 00:01:06.940
- Delia tell the truth.
- It used to scare me but not anymore.

00:01:07.312 --> 00:01:10.509
That's what she says every time
like a junkie begging for more smack.

00:01:10.682 --> 00:01:12.445
I'm not a junkie! You're a junkie!

00:01:12.618 --> 00:01:15.451
No one's a junkie in this house! Yet.

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:19.921
Dr. Brown.

00:01:21.159 --> 00:01:22.922
Yes. Yes I can.

00:01:23.362 --> 00:01:26.798
We're just finishing dinner now.
I'll be right over. What's your address?

00:01:26.965 --> 00:01:30.662
Okay then. See you in a bit. Will do.

00:01:32.004 --> 00:01:34.973
- Who was that?
- What I've been waiting for since we came.

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:38.075
- My first house call.
- "We're just finishing dinner" huh?

00:01:38.243 --> 00:01:41.303
Well I can't let my first
house-call family feel bad Ephram.

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:43.778
Wouldn't be very country-doctorly
of me would it?

00:01:44.216 --> 00:01:45.979
Besides I won't be long.

00:01:46.151 --> 00:01:49.018
- Is a knapsack country-doctorly?
- Good point Delia.

00:01:49.187 --> 00:01:53.317
I need something that says
"country doctor." I know an umbrella!

00:01:53.492 --> 00:01:57.656
- That says "singing English nanny."
- Never mind. I'll see you guys later.

00:01:57.829 --> 00:01:59.888
Remember save me a piece
of that meat loaf.

00:02:00.065 --> 00:02:01.965
Without a doubt.

00:02:02.834 --> 00:02:05.394
- I'll order pizza.
- Half cheese half pepperoni.

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:13.776
- Mrs. Dudley I presume.
- Evening doctor.

00:02:13.945 --> 00:02:17.039
- I see you found the place.
- It took me longer than I thought.

00:02:17.449 --> 00:02:19.713
Just out of curiosity
how long is Forest Lane?

00:02:19.885 --> 00:02:21.182
Fifteen miles.

00:02:21.353 --> 00:02:23.253
Where I come from that's a turnpike.

00:02:24.589 --> 00:02:27.490
I was just about to put on some coffee
if you'd like a cup.

00:02:27.893 --> 00:02:31.989
No thanks. So which one's the patient?

00:02:32.164 --> 00:02:34.894
- You don't charge right?
- That's right.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:36.899
All of them.

00:03:26.551 --> 00:03:28.781
<i>Yes, the chocolate,</i>
<i>but that's just the beginning.</i>

00:03:28.954 --> 00:03:32.651
<i>We have to get on. We have to get on.</i>
<i>We have so much time and so little to do.</i>

00:03:32.824 --> 00:03:34.587
S<i>trike that. Reverse it.</i>

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:36.421
<i>This way, please.</i>

00:03:37.095 --> 00:03:38.995
<i>We'll take the wonkavator.</i>

00:04:00.685 --> 00:04:02.516
Hey Dad.

00:04:02.921 --> 00:04:04.582
Hey kiddo.

00:04:04.756 --> 00:04:08.157
- How was the movie?
- I tried not to watch it honest.

00:04:08.326 --> 00:04:09.987
But it called out to me.

00:04:11.196 --> 00:04:12.891
- I bet.
- I didn't get scared.

00:04:13.064 --> 00:04:16.625
I even watched the part
where the girl turns into a blueberry...

00:04:16.802 --> 00:04:21.136
...which you and I both know
isn't really possible. Is it?

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:25.637
Well there was one reported case
in Norway in the late '60s...

00:04:25.811 --> 00:04:27.403
...but I wouldn't worry about it.

00:04:27.579 --> 00:04:29.479
Go back to sleep.

00:04:35.253 --> 00:04:36.777
I'm back.

00:04:37.656 --> 00:04:39.146
Sound the trumpets.

00:04:41.393 --> 00:04:43.122
I know it took longer than expected.

00:04:43.295 --> 00:04:45.160
I hadn't really noticed.

00:04:45.797 --> 00:04:47.389
The door?

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:34.840
It's a vacation Andy
you gonna spend it all cleaning?

00:05:35.013 --> 00:05:36.674
I was just straightening up.

00:05:36.848 --> 00:05:40.784
Admit it the great Dr. Brown
can't sit still.

00:05:40.952 --> 00:05:42.749
You need to do settle down with a book.

00:05:42.921 --> 00:05:45.583
Like <i>Madame Bovary?</i>
There's some light summer fare.

00:05:47.092 --> 00:05:48.491
Now about your son...

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:52.562
That argument tonight was not my fault.
Did you hear the way he talked to me?

00:05:52.731 --> 00:05:55.632
He's a teenager. Sarcasm is how
they express their affection.

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:58.860
- Well he's got a funny way of expressing it.
- And your way isn't?

00:05:59.037 --> 00:06:03.371
You take one week of family vacation
a year and you spend it cleaning.

00:06:03.541 --> 00:06:06.533
- The garage the kitchen...
- I asked him to go in the boat today.

00:06:06.711 --> 00:06:09.612
He didn't want to go. Okay?

00:06:09.781 --> 00:06:11.749
I was gonna teach him how to drive it.

00:06:11.917 --> 00:06:15.409
Teaching him something isn't
the only way to get to know him.

00:06:15.587 --> 00:06:19.455
When I was his age I would have killed
for my father to teach me to drive a boat.

00:06:19.624 --> 00:06:21.182
I would've killed to have a boat.

00:06:21.993 --> 00:06:25.360
I swear to God one day you two
are gonna understand each other...

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:28.055
...if it's the last thing I ever do.

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:31.233
Well if that's your goal
you're gonna be around a while.

00:06:38.576 --> 00:06:42.034
- Hey Nina.
- Evening Andy.

00:06:53.725 --> 00:06:56.922
Sometimes I remember
conversations with my wife.

00:06:57.095 --> 00:06:58.562
And this one...?

00:06:59.497 --> 00:07:01.988
It was a talk we had last year.

00:07:02.801 --> 00:07:05.031
We had a house in the Hamptons.

00:07:05.203 --> 00:07:07.797
She'd take the kids for the summer.

00:07:08.573 --> 00:07:12.100
Me I was there a total
of three weeks in five years.

00:07:12.777 --> 00:07:17.339
And yourself? I assume you're not
out here talking to a deceased spouse.

00:07:17.515 --> 00:07:20.484
No just enjoying the warm night.

00:07:20.652 --> 00:07:23.985
Which is unseasonably warm considering
we had a snowstorm last week.

00:07:24.155 --> 00:07:26.555
- Oh it's the fall thaw.
- Excuse me?

00:07:26.725 --> 00:07:29.159
Welcome to one of Everwood's
many oddities.

00:07:29.327 --> 00:07:30.817
There's a fall thaw?

00:07:30.996 --> 00:07:32.623
With a legend behind it no less.

00:07:33.365 --> 00:07:37.096
Once a year like clockwork we get
a fall heat wave that lasts around a week...

00:07:37.268 --> 00:07:39.793
...and the town whips up a festival
to celebrate it.

00:07:39.971 --> 00:07:41.962
I'm gonna stop you
before this gets weirder.

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:43.505
Oh you think that's weird?

00:07:43.675 --> 00:07:46.337
Last week we got a doctor
who doesn't charge anybody.

00:07:48.279 --> 00:07:52.181
- Good night Andy.
- Good night Nina.

00:07:57.188 --> 00:08:01.625
<i>The next day, as the temperature climbed,</i>
<i>so did the town's excitement.</i>

00:08:01.793 --> 00:08:05.422
<i>Looking around, it was almost impossible</i>
<i>to imagine anyone in Everwood...</i>

00:08:05.597 --> 00:08:08.532
<i>... not happy about the recent turn</i>
<i>in temperature.</i>

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:12.158
<i>Notice I said, "almost."</i>

00:08:13.638 --> 00:08:16.334
You there! Yes sign boy
I'm talking to you.

00:08:16.508 --> 00:08:19.909
If you're gonna hang that banner
off my building don't chip the paint.

00:08:20.078 --> 00:08:24.913
That is Benjamin Moore latex
the Rolls-Royce of exterior coatings.

00:08:27.552 --> 00:08:28.917
Morning doctor.

00:08:29.421 --> 00:08:31.889
- Happy thaw.
- You're an educated man doctor.

00:08:32.057 --> 00:08:36.016
You don't plan on succumbing to one
of this community's nonsensical traditions?

00:08:36.194 --> 00:08:39.129
You gotta admit
it's a balmy day for mid-September.

00:08:39.297 --> 00:08:43.028
The weather pattern we experience this
time of year is a typical Indian summer...

00:08:43.201 --> 00:08:45.431
...brought by a flow
of the polar jet stream...

00:08:45.603 --> 00:08:49.198
...which with our proximity to the
mountains in turn traps and stagnates...

00:08:49.374 --> 00:08:51.740
...the hottest air directly above our region.

00:08:51.943 --> 00:08:55.879
And as much as this town enjoys
celebrating this anomaly...

00:08:56.047 --> 00:09:01.246
...for us sensitive to the allergens in
the air this is not much of a fun week.

00:09:01.419 --> 00:09:04.786
As opposed to all those other weeks
where you just like to party down?

00:09:04.956 --> 00:09:09.393
As usual you make it difficult to have
a civil conversation with you doctor.

00:09:09.894 --> 00:09:12.658
- Thaw well.
- Bite me.

00:09:13.598 --> 00:09:16.226
- Morning everyone.
- Morning!

00:09:16.668 --> 00:09:19.068
You're late. They're getting
hotter than a hooker's...

00:09:19.237 --> 00:09:22.604
Don't finish that analogy Edna.
I haven't had my coffee yet.

00:09:22.774 --> 00:09:25.572
- Late night?
- I answered my first house call.

00:09:25.743 --> 00:09:27.802
Oh you finally busted the old cherry.

00:09:27.979 --> 00:09:29.776
- Who with?
- The Dudleys.

00:09:29.948 --> 00:09:31.916
- On Forest Lane?
- It was no lane.

00:09:32.083 --> 00:09:35.951
Took me half an hour to find the place
another hour and a half to examine her kids.

00:09:36.121 --> 00:09:39.420
I hope you got some rest.
We got ourselves another packed house.

00:09:39.591 --> 00:09:41.718
Oh it never lets up Edna does it?

00:09:41.893 --> 00:09:47.798
Remind me and my tired feet why you are
offering this thankless town free medicine.

00:09:48.533 --> 00:09:52.765
Long answer is I spent enough years
making money off people's sickness.

00:09:52.937 --> 00:09:56.896
In order to assuage my guilt I wanted
to do something incredibly altruistic.

00:09:57.075 --> 00:09:58.440
The short answer is...

00:09:58.610 --> 00:09:59.838
...l'm nuts.

00:10:02.780 --> 00:10:04.407
Okay give it to me.

00:10:04.582 --> 00:10:06.482
- Excuse me?
- Your academic update.

00:10:06.651 --> 00:10:09.176
You've been here a week.
What do you think of classes?

00:10:09.354 --> 00:10:12.346
I think they're as annoying and dull
as my classes in New York...

00:10:12.524 --> 00:10:14.822
...only further west.

00:10:15.326 --> 00:10:18.420
I'll warn you there's a movement
to issue the new kid a nickname.

00:10:18.596 --> 00:10:20.962
Why do I not like the direction
this is going?

00:10:21.132 --> 00:10:25.762
It's an offensive tactic. The way I see it
as the new kid you'll get a nickname.

00:10:25.937 --> 00:10:29.703
These labels are never kind.
They're either fun or mean.

00:10:29.874 --> 00:10:31.603
- Most are mean.
- I know.

00:10:31.776 --> 00:10:34.973
- I have gym with "Blackhead" Davis.
- See what I mean?

00:10:35.146 --> 00:10:37.944
Now if you annihilate the few
suggested nicknames...

00:10:38.116 --> 00:10:40.107
...we have a shot
at making a fun one stick.

00:10:40.318 --> 00:10:43.685
You know for the classic girl-next-door
you have a really warped mind.

00:10:44.522 --> 00:10:46.217
- It's something in the water.
- So...

00:10:46.391 --> 00:10:49.360
...what's yours?
- Me? They call me...

00:10:50.328 --> 00:10:52.057
Late for class!

00:10:52.230 --> 00:10:53.891
- See you bubba.
- Bubba?

00:10:54.065 --> 00:10:55.794
Just testing one out.

00:11:02.607 --> 00:11:04.336
Well howdy loser.

00:11:04.509 --> 00:11:07.478
You guys choreograph the
bathroom-stall exit and I'm the loser?

00:11:07.645 --> 00:11:10.205
I see you're still getting cozy
with my little sis.

00:11:10.381 --> 00:11:11.973
I told you once she's spoken for.

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:16.052
"Spoken for"? Hey Bright the '50s called
they want their lingo back.

00:11:18.623 --> 00:11:22.081
As soon as Colin finds out about you
he's gonna kick your sorry ass.

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:27.197
I figure I might have a slight advantage
over him seeing as I'm conscious.

00:11:27.365 --> 00:11:29.856
Watch what you say little man.

00:11:30.034 --> 00:11:32.764
Another comment Colin won't be
the only one in a coma.

00:11:32.937 --> 00:11:37.772
Statistically I'm not little but according to
every chart I've seen you're still a moron.

00:11:37.942 --> 00:11:39.773
Oh you may think I'm a moron.

00:11:39.944 --> 00:11:42.970
You may be right. When it comes
to my sister Amy I'm a genius.

00:11:43.147 --> 00:11:45.047
And she's playing you dude.

00:11:45.216 --> 00:11:49.414
Soon as she gets your daddy fixing up
Colin she's not even going to look at you.

00:11:51.189 --> 00:11:52.918
Just remember I said that.

00:12:04.535 --> 00:12:10.167
And that children is how Ronald Reagan
saved the world from the evil empire.

00:12:10.341 --> 00:12:12.832
Yes Delia what is it now?

00:12:13.011 --> 00:12:16.447
I can't see the board as well from here.
Can I move up front?

00:12:16.814 --> 00:12:18.748
Is there something wrong with your eyes?

00:12:18.916 --> 00:12:21.510
- No.
- Then why do you need to sit up front?

00:12:21.853 --> 00:12:23.184
To hear you better.

00:12:23.354 --> 00:12:25.288
Oh you have a hearing difficulty?

00:12:25.456 --> 00:12:26.718
No.

00:12:26.891 --> 00:12:29.382
I'm sorry Delia I don't understand.

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:31.391
I just like to sit close.

00:12:32.497 --> 00:12:35.330
In this class the boys
sit in the front rows...

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:38.230
...and the girls sit in the other rows.

00:12:38.403 --> 00:12:40.997
- You mean the back rows.
- Yes.

00:12:41.172 --> 00:12:45.336
Now if everyone will turn
in their reading books to page 86...

00:12:45.510 --> 00:12:46.875
Do we ever switch?

00:12:47.045 --> 00:12:50.037
- Excuse me?
- Do the boys and girls ever switch?

00:12:51.115 --> 00:12:54.243
- No.
- Then I'd like to sit up front please.

00:12:54.419 --> 00:12:55.647
I see.

00:12:55.820 --> 00:12:58.687
Well to do that you'd have to be a boy.

00:12:58.856 --> 00:13:03.054
You're not suggesting that you
really are a boy Delia are you?

00:13:05.496 --> 00:13:06.827
I didn't think so.

00:13:08.266 --> 00:13:10.734
And while we're at it remove your hat.

00:13:10.902 --> 00:13:14.770
This is a classroom not a ball field.

00:13:18.076 --> 00:13:20.306
I said remove your hat.

00:13:21.813 --> 00:13:23.144
Delia.

00:13:23.781 --> 00:13:25.009
Delia!

00:13:25.350 --> 00:13:30.515
<i>Welcome to Gino Chang's,</i>
<i>Everwood's Friday-night culinary hot spot.</i>

00:13:30.955 --> 00:13:35.824
<i>Gino, the restaurant's proprietor, moved</i>
<i>to town from Naples a few years back.</i>

00:13:35.993 --> 00:13:40.293
<i>At the time, Everwood was without</i>
<i>a Chinese restaurant or an Italian one.</i>

00:13:40.465 --> 00:13:42.330
S<i>o Gino opened both.</i>

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:47.028
We'll have one order of the minestrone
two orders of the chicken parmigiana...

00:13:47.472 --> 00:13:49.201
...one sweet-and-sour pork...

00:13:49.974 --> 00:13:51.839
...and a couple of egg rolls to start.

00:13:52.009 --> 00:13:57.140
I'd like to point out that this is the
weirdest restaurant we've ever been to...

00:13:57.315 --> 00:14:00.478
...and we're from New York City
where we're served by drag queens.

00:14:00.651 --> 00:14:02.050
I think it's cool.

00:14:02.220 --> 00:14:04.848
So who's up for going
to the Thaw Fest tomorrow?

00:14:05.022 --> 00:14:08.822
I'd love to as long as you promise to
take up surgery and lobotomize me first.

00:14:08.993 --> 00:14:12.451
Come on Ephram it'll be fun.
There's gonna be hayrides a Ferris wheel.

00:14:12.630 --> 00:14:15.258
In what universe does that
translate into "fun"?

00:14:15.433 --> 00:14:19.802
Dad what's it mean when someone
takes "extreme disciplinary measures"?

00:14:19.971 --> 00:14:22.462
- Where'd you hear that expression?
- On TV.

00:14:22.874 --> 00:14:24.239
It means someone's in trouble.

00:14:26.844 --> 00:14:30.007
Dr. Abbott
Everwood's big shot tough guy!

00:14:30.181 --> 00:14:33.412
- How are we doing tonight?
- Fine Gino. Our regular table please.

00:14:33.584 --> 00:14:36.212
I'm sorry. Your regular table
she no avail this evening.

00:14:36.387 --> 00:14:38.378
What do you mean "She no avail"?

00:14:38.556 --> 00:14:42.083
Have no worry. I'm gonna give you
a <i>bellissimo</i> table right in the corner.

00:14:42.260 --> 00:14:45.491
Gino I do not want a <i>bellissimo</i> table.
I want my regular table.

00:14:45.663 --> 00:14:47.961
As a dedicated patron
of this establishment...

00:14:48.132 --> 00:14:53.570
...I find it appalling you would just jettison
my table without any regard whatsoever.

00:14:54.605 --> 00:14:58.200
You smarty-pants doctor
I no get your fancy words.

00:14:58.376 --> 00:15:02.176
But tonight the dessert
she's on the house.

00:15:05.516 --> 00:15:08.383
Hey Ephram how's it going
with the Abbott girl?

00:15:08.753 --> 00:15:10.414
- What brought that up?
- Just curious.

00:15:10.588 --> 00:15:12.249
- Don't be.
- It must be going well...

00:15:12.423 --> 00:15:13.754
...she's walking over here.

00:15:14.959 --> 00:15:17.393
- Hey bubba.
- Dad you remember Amy.

00:15:17.562 --> 00:15:19.962
- Of course. Hello Amy.
- Hello Dr. Brown.

00:15:20.465 --> 00:15:23.059
My boyfriend is in a stage-4 coma
and I was wondering...

00:15:23.234 --> 00:15:26.965
...if you would consider using your talents
in neurosurgery to help awaken him...

00:15:27.138 --> 00:15:29.902
...from his severe head trauma
so that I can sleep with him.

00:15:30.074 --> 00:15:32.201
I'd be glad to.

00:15:33.644 --> 00:15:35.635
Dad you remember Amy.

00:15:35.813 --> 00:15:38.407
- Hey there Amy.
- Hi. What's your name?

00:15:38.583 --> 00:15:40.278
I'm Delia. You're pretty.

00:15:41.786 --> 00:15:44.186
Hello? Hello? This is he.

00:15:44.355 --> 00:15:47.813
- So you're just here with your dad?
- Yeah. How'd you know?

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:51.060
He's kind of hard to miss.

00:15:51.229 --> 00:15:54.630
It's father-daughter night so we eat
and go home and watch something...

00:15:54.799 --> 00:15:58.098
...he's taped off of Turner Classics.
- Sounds bitchen.

00:15:58.269 --> 00:16:00.760
I know it's hard to believe
but he can be cool...

00:16:00.938 --> 00:16:02.803
...when no one's looking.
- Amy? Hello.

00:16:02.974 --> 00:16:06.671
Anyways I better get back before
he combusts. I just wanted to say hi.

00:16:06.844 --> 00:16:08.436
- See you.
- See you.

00:16:09.247 --> 00:16:11.238
Is she your girlfriend?

00:16:11.415 --> 00:16:13.246
- No.
- But you want her to be.

00:16:13.417 --> 00:16:16.045
You're close to knowing pain
you've never known before.

00:16:16.254 --> 00:16:18.814
That was my patient.
I've gotta get right over there.

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:20.981
- It's an emergency.
- We just ordered.

00:16:22.226 --> 00:16:24.820
I should be back by the time
you finish okay?

00:16:24.996 --> 00:16:27.556
Look I'll tell you what
here's money for dinner.

00:16:27.732 --> 00:16:29.666
And you can use my phone to call a cab.

00:16:29.834 --> 00:16:32.098
- Can you do that Ephram?
- Sure thing Pops.

00:16:32.270 --> 00:16:34.500
Look I'm sorry guys.
I'll make it up to you.

00:16:34.672 --> 00:16:37.368
I promise I won't cook dinner
for a whole week.

00:16:40.111 --> 00:16:41.476
<i>Not working tonight?</i>

00:16:41.646 --> 00:16:44.774
It took me 20 minutes just
to track this number down.

00:16:45.316 --> 00:16:50.720
Look at this. Now what kind of a father
leaves his children in a restaurant alone?

00:16:51.756 --> 00:16:53.451
Stranded?

00:16:53.624 --> 00:16:55.251
Just trying to get a taxi.

00:16:55.426 --> 00:16:58.862
It turns out there's only one cabby in town
and he's taken the night off.

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:02.727
Mr. Randolph. He doesn't work Friday
nights he calls bingo numbers at church.

00:17:02.900 --> 00:17:04.868
This really is the town that time forgot.

00:17:05.036 --> 00:17:08.062
We can give you a ride home.
Right Daddy?

00:17:10.474 --> 00:17:12.169
Of course we can.

00:17:16.614 --> 00:17:18.844
He sits up front with me.

00:17:19.917 --> 00:17:21.214
Good boy.

00:17:21.385 --> 00:17:24.047
It doesn't make sense.
Susie was the one with the cough.

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:27.487
What appears to have been bronchitis...

00:17:27.658 --> 00:17:30.650
...is bacterial pneumococci
which is a silly way to say...

00:17:30.828 --> 00:17:33.319
..."infectious pneumonia"
which is not silly at all.

00:17:33.497 --> 00:17:36.261
- He's got pneumonia?
- He does.

00:17:36.434 --> 00:17:40.427
Judging by the tightness of the quarters
here my guess is all your kids are infected.

00:17:40.605 --> 00:17:43.096
On the off-chance they're not
I've got vaccinations.

00:17:43.274 --> 00:17:46.038
Unfortunately I don't have
any antibiotics with me.

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:49.771
- You can give him a dose of Susie's tonight.
- I'm sorry I can't do that.

00:17:49.947 --> 00:17:51.778
It's perfectly allowable Mrs. Dudley.

00:17:51.949 --> 00:17:54.884
I could write a separate prescription
and you can pick it up...

00:17:55.052 --> 00:17:57.486
- I never got Susie's medicine.
- I'm sorry?

00:17:57.655 --> 00:18:00.055
Our truck's been out of commission
for a few months.

00:18:00.224 --> 00:18:04.217
I was gonna have my sister drive me.
She doesn't get back until next Tuesday.

00:18:04.395 --> 00:18:08.126
Mrs. Dudley your son doesn't need
antibiotics on Tuesday he needs them now.

00:18:08.733 --> 00:18:12.191
You said yourself that Susie's cough
was mild so I thought it could wait.

00:18:12.370 --> 00:18:16.568
Well it can't wait the night not unless you
want to spend tomorrow at the hospital.

00:18:21.112 --> 00:18:22.636
Okay.

00:18:22.813 --> 00:18:25.941
Get your kids ready. We're gonna
go find the nearest pharmacy.

00:18:26.117 --> 00:18:28.381
- Dr. Brown I can't let you do that.
- You have to.

00:18:28.552 --> 00:18:31.077
- Why?
- Because your children are sick.

00:18:31.255 --> 00:18:33.985
Because I should have diagnosed
them properly days ago.

00:18:34.158 --> 00:18:37.252
Because I have a car and you don't.
But mostly because...

00:18:38.062 --> 00:18:40.030
...l'm your doctor.

00:18:40.297 --> 00:18:41.924
Now come on.

00:18:44.301 --> 00:18:47.236
Thanks for the ride Dr. Abbott.

00:18:50.441 --> 00:18:53.069
Thaw Fest is tomorrow.
I was wondering if you were going.

00:18:53.244 --> 00:18:56.407
- Ephram?
- Just a second.

00:18:57.314 --> 00:19:01.148
I'm thinking about going. I hear
they have hayrides and Ferris wheels.

00:19:01.318 --> 00:19:03.878
Did you know they have
a horseshoe-throwing competition?

00:19:04.055 --> 00:19:06.922
- Ephram!
- I said just a second!

00:19:07.091 --> 00:19:09.321
Little sisters you know.

00:19:09.794 --> 00:19:12.695
But yeah no I was thinking
about going to the Festival...

00:19:12.863 --> 00:19:14.922
...of the Thaw.

00:19:15.099 --> 00:19:17.226
That came out wrong.

00:19:17.401 --> 00:19:18.959
- Two o'clock.
- Ephram!

00:19:20.104 --> 00:19:21.696
Bye.

00:19:25.142 --> 00:19:27.474
- What?
- We're locked out.

00:19:30.748 --> 00:19:34.980
Over my dead and decaying corpse
you're going to Thaw Fest with that boy.

00:19:35.152 --> 00:19:37.882
I am not going with him
I am just meeting him there.

00:19:38.055 --> 00:19:40.319
Since when do you care
who I go to Thaw Fest with?

00:19:40.491 --> 00:19:43.483
Since you started asking future
parolees to attend with you.

00:19:43.661 --> 00:19:44.889
You don't know him.

00:19:45.362 --> 00:19:48.263
- This is so unfair!
- Well in certain parent-child conflicts...

00:19:48.432 --> 00:19:49.899
...fairness is irrelevant.

00:19:50.067 --> 00:19:53.059
Why is it the parent that always
gets to decide the relevancy?

00:19:53.237 --> 00:19:56.934
- Excellent question if I do say so myself.
- Hello dear.

00:19:57.108 --> 00:19:59.804
Mom Dad is being excruciating!

00:19:59.977 --> 00:20:02.878
"Excruciating" literally means
to feel the pain of crucifixion.

00:20:03.047 --> 00:20:05.015
While my law may be difficult at times...

00:20:05.182 --> 00:20:08.709
...I think we can both agree
that Jesus had it a bit tougher.

00:20:08.886 --> 00:20:10.854
He didn't live here!

00:20:11.021 --> 00:20:12.488
What...? Now...

00:20:12.656 --> 00:20:17.252
Where are you going? We haven't gotten
to the movie half yet. It's your favorite.

00:20:17.428 --> 00:20:19.225
Repeat viewing of <i>The Red</i> S<i>hoes</i>.

00:20:19.730 --> 00:20:22.062
Oh don't look at me like that.

00:20:22.233 --> 00:20:24.929
- Like you're gonna overrule me.
- I don't have to.

00:20:25.102 --> 00:20:26.899
You're gonna rescind your own ruling.

00:20:27.071 --> 00:20:30.404
Our daughter hasn't had a moment's fun
since Colin's accident.

00:20:30.574 --> 00:20:34.032
Now if she wanted to go to that festival
with Eminem I'd let her do it.

00:20:34.211 --> 00:20:36.202
Rose do you know who this boy is?

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:40.441
He's the son of that faux Marcus Welby.

00:20:40.618 --> 00:20:43.849
You'll be interested to know
we had another five cancellations today!

00:20:44.021 --> 00:20:48.481
"Just feeling better Dr. Abbott"
they all say. Yeah give me a break.

00:20:48.659 --> 00:20:52.356
Like Marion Wattle's
biliary cirrhosis just healed itself.

00:20:52.530 --> 00:20:56.193
Come on! They're all going across
the street for some free medicine.

00:20:57.701 --> 00:20:59.692
And how can I compete with that?

00:20:59.870 --> 00:21:03.033
We've had this conversation
umpteen times Harold.

00:21:03.207 --> 00:21:04.697
This isn't about that doctor...

00:21:04.875 --> 00:21:07.139
...or his son or even about free medicine.

00:21:07.311 --> 00:21:09.541
You know what this is about.

00:21:10.047 --> 00:21:11.947
This is not about my mother.

00:21:12.383 --> 00:21:15.352
I couldn't care less
what that battle-ax does.

00:21:15.519 --> 00:21:18.818
Her working there is just another attempt
meant to embarrass me...

00:21:18.989 --> 00:21:22.618
...and it'll prove just as ineffective
as all the others.

00:21:24.728 --> 00:21:26.696
Good night Harold.

00:21:32.670 --> 00:21:34.001
Delia Brown...

00:21:34.305 --> 00:21:37.206
...what did I tell you about hats in class?

00:21:37.641 --> 00:21:39.768
- No hats in class.
- That's right.

00:21:40.377 --> 00:21:44.438
- No hats in class! No hats in class!
- Miss Violet you're turning violet!

00:21:46.984 --> 00:21:49.418
<i>No hats in class! No hats in class!</i>

00:21:49.587 --> 00:21:53.079
She's gonna explode!
She's gonna explode!

00:21:53.257 --> 00:21:56.055
- She's gonna explode!
- Delia what's wrong?

00:21:56.227 --> 00:21:58.957
- Miss Violet's gonna explode!
- Nobody's gonna explode.

00:21:59.129 --> 00:22:02.690
- Where's Dad? I want Dad.
- He'll be home soon. Here lie down.

00:22:02.867 --> 00:22:04.630
Okay?

00:22:08.205 --> 00:22:11.299
- Ephram?
- Yes?

00:22:11.475 --> 00:22:14.273
Could you stay with me for a little while?

00:22:17.248 --> 00:22:19.239
Move over.

00:22:41.405 --> 00:22:43.202
Where have you been?

00:22:43.374 --> 00:22:46.901
I was stuck at the Dudleys. Why
what's the matter? Everything okay?

00:22:47.077 --> 00:22:50.046
No everything's not okay.
Your daughter had a nightmare tonight.

00:22:50.381 --> 00:22:53.043
- How is she?
- She's fine now.

00:22:53.217 --> 00:22:55.651
Got her back to sleep
about 30 minutes ago.

00:22:56.186 --> 00:23:00.350
It was that movie wasn't it?
I should have made sure she didn't see it.

00:23:00.524 --> 00:23:03.391
For someone who was cited
by <i>U.</i>S<i>. News & World Report</i>...

00:23:03.560 --> 00:23:07.291
...as "one of the greatest minds in
America" I'm amazed how clueless you are.

00:23:07.464 --> 00:23:09.523
You really think this was about a movie?

00:23:09.700 --> 00:23:12.863
Well why don't you enlighten me
Ephram as to what it is about...

00:23:13.037 --> 00:23:16.495
...because what I need tonight is another
lecture from my 15-year-old son.

00:23:16.674 --> 00:23:19.370
Don't talk to me like you talked to Mom.
I'm not your wife.

00:23:19.543 --> 00:23:22.944
- What's that supposed to mean?
- You think I wanna have this conversation?

00:23:23.113 --> 00:23:25.741
I didn't marry you.
I never agreed to pick up your slack.

00:23:25.950 --> 00:23:29.283
Look Ephram I am sorry I couldn't
take care of Delia tonight...

00:23:29.453 --> 00:23:32.581
...but I was treating a 7-year-old boy
who could hardly breathe.

00:23:32.756 --> 00:23:36.248
You win! Seven-year-old boys who can't
breathe trump girls with nightmares.

00:23:36.427 --> 00:23:40.124
- Yes in my profession they do.
- The medical one or the crappy-father one?

00:23:40.297 --> 00:23:42.663
All right that is enough!

00:23:42.833 --> 00:23:46.394
As of this second you and that mouth
are gonna start showing me respect or...

00:23:46.570 --> 00:23:47.935
Or what?

00:23:48.806 --> 00:23:50.774
What happened to your hand?

00:23:50.941 --> 00:23:55.105
It's tonight's punch line. I sliced it while
trying to pry open a window to this place...

00:23:55.279 --> 00:23:57.577
...which happened after
we couldn't get a ride...

00:23:57.748 --> 00:24:00.808
...after you left us at dinner
for the second night this week!

00:24:00.985 --> 00:24:02.543
- Let me take a look.
- It's fine.

00:24:02.720 --> 00:24:05.416
- Let me just see it.
- Don't touch me!

00:24:07.925 --> 00:24:11.986
"The great Dr. Brown."
That's what Mom and I used to call you.

00:24:12.162 --> 00:24:15.131
You always thought it was endearing
but it wasn't.

00:24:15.299 --> 00:24:17.324
It was our own private joke.

00:24:17.501 --> 00:24:19.366
"Will the great Dr. Brown be at dinner?"

00:24:19.536 --> 00:24:21.697
"Will the great Dr. Brown
join us this weekend?"

00:24:21.872 --> 00:24:23.737
Don't you see? You're still that guy.

00:24:23.907 --> 00:24:27.104
You'll always be that guy.
Whether it's the Dudleys on Forest Lane...

00:24:27.277 --> 00:24:31.179
...or some rich lady on Park Avenue
they'll always come first.

00:24:31.782 --> 00:24:34.910
Only difference is this time
Mom's not here to cover for you.

00:24:35.452 --> 00:24:37.352
At least I got her.

00:24:38.389 --> 00:24:40.254
Who does Delia get?

00:25:04.548 --> 00:25:06.846
Now what did we talk about in the car?

00:25:07.017 --> 00:25:10.475
- For the next three hours I don't know you.
- Good.

00:25:10.654 --> 00:25:12.781
- Hey Edna!
- Remember my main squeeze Irv?

00:25:12.956 --> 00:25:14.287
- Good to see you Irv.
- Hello.

00:25:14.458 --> 00:25:16.426
- Hello there Delia.
- Hey Mr. Irv.

00:25:16.593 --> 00:25:18.823
Doc Brown Thurman Revere
from Glen Oaks Drive.

00:25:18.996 --> 00:25:23.023
- Hi Thurman. How are you?
- Listen I have a cyst above my backside.

00:25:23.200 --> 00:25:27.432
- Well Thurman I'm here with my family...
- It's a quick look-see. It'd take a second.

00:25:27.604 --> 00:25:29.299
- Well Thurman...
- Go ahead doc.

00:25:29.506 --> 00:25:31.406
We'll watch the munchkin for a bit.

00:25:32.376 --> 00:25:34.776
All right. No not here Thurman.

00:25:47.124 --> 00:25:49.149
- Hey.
- Hey there you are.

00:25:49.326 --> 00:25:52.818
Ephram Brown the melting man.
The melting man Ephram Brown.

00:25:53.097 --> 00:25:55.327
- He's oddly quiet.
- He's not having the best day.

00:25:55.499 --> 00:25:56.932
I think it might be his last.

00:25:57.101 --> 00:25:59.399
Everyone just watches him melt?

00:25:59.570 --> 00:26:02.232
It's a contest. You bet when
the hat will hit the ground.

00:26:02.406 --> 00:26:04.465
Mr. Lawrence there won
three years in a row.

00:26:04.641 --> 00:26:07.132
I think it's safe to say
we have a few hours yet.

00:26:08.545 --> 00:26:11.241
Here's the deal. My dad agreed
I could hang with you...

00:26:11.415 --> 00:26:13.815
...under one condition.
- Yeah? What's that?

00:26:14.818 --> 00:26:16.308
How goes it bone lick?

00:26:17.955 --> 00:26:19.684
He has to hang with us.

00:26:19.857 --> 00:26:21.449
No offense Amy...

00:26:21.625 --> 00:26:24.093
...but he's really my least
favorite thing about you.

00:26:24.261 --> 00:26:27.753
Well you're really my least
favorite thing about you.

00:26:27.931 --> 00:26:29.558
You gotta work on the insults.

00:26:30.334 --> 00:26:34.828
So what are we gonna do first?
We got face painting over there.

00:26:35.005 --> 00:26:36.666
Let's try the silent auction here.

00:26:38.575 --> 00:26:41.066
Vanilla and chocolate
frozen yogurt in a cup...

00:26:41.245 --> 00:26:44.578
...with a spoon-and-a-half of sprinkles
distributed evenly over the top.

00:26:44.748 --> 00:26:46.716
Make sure to rinse that sprinkle spoon...

00:26:46.884 --> 00:26:50.581
Buddy how about you finish ordering
before the thaw's gone.

00:26:50.754 --> 00:26:52.187
Hello Mother.

00:26:52.356 --> 00:26:54.290
How's it hanging Junior?

00:26:54.458 --> 00:26:56.449
With the plethora of greetings
in English...

00:26:56.627 --> 00:26:58.720
...I find it hard to believe that's the best.

00:26:58.896 --> 00:27:01.194
I find it hard to believe
you use "plethora."

00:27:01.365 --> 00:27:03.299
Two scoops of chocolate
on a cone please.

00:27:05.936 --> 00:27:09.497
You got your panties in a bunch we're
gonna steal your patients don't worry.

00:27:09.673 --> 00:27:13.803
There's enough hoity-toities around
these parts who don't want to wait...

00:27:13.977 --> 00:27:17.242
...in the same room with folks
from the wrong side of the mountain.

00:27:17.414 --> 00:27:19.211
I do not have my panties in a bunch.

00:27:19.383 --> 00:27:21.943
- lf you must know I'm concerned for you.
- Concerned?

00:27:22.119 --> 00:27:24.019
You're working with
an addled human being.

00:27:24.188 --> 00:27:28.124
Considering you've had bouts with reality
too I don't recommend the exposure.

00:27:28.292 --> 00:27:30.920
- What are these bouts?
- How about the time you decided...

00:27:31.094 --> 00:27:34.222
...to leap your motorbike over four cars
down Main Street?

00:27:34.398 --> 00:27:37.128
That was a fundraiser
for Myrna Sander's goiter operation.

00:27:37.301 --> 00:27:41.237
How about this drunken bar brawl
last month with Edgar Cage?

00:27:41.405 --> 00:27:43.339
Edgar had it coming. He called me a puss.

00:27:43.507 --> 00:27:45.907
Your sophomoric stunts aside
the truth is Mother...

00:27:46.076 --> 00:27:50.137
...you've given no thought to the fact that
you may be driving into an early grave.

00:27:50.347 --> 00:27:53.839
You'd like that too. Then you could say
to my corpse "I told you so."

00:27:54.017 --> 00:27:56.417
You're presuming I'd attend your funeral.

00:27:56.587 --> 00:27:58.487
You know what your trouble is Junior?

00:27:58.655 --> 00:28:01.818
Your whole life you've wanted
this town to see you...

00:28:01.992 --> 00:28:03.983
...the same way they saw your pops:

00:28:04.161 --> 00:28:07.653
Wise generous big-hearted.

00:28:07.831 --> 00:28:09.321
Trouble is...

00:28:09.499 --> 00:28:12.127
...people can't see what's not there.

00:28:12.669 --> 00:28:18.164
As usual I'm bathed in your
maternal warmth and kindness.

00:28:33.357 --> 00:28:36.190
I'm surprised Bright didn't charm
himself up here with us.

00:28:36.360 --> 00:28:39.693
I knew he wouldn't go near this thing.
He's deathly afraid of heights.

00:28:39.863 --> 00:28:41.763
So what do people do up here...

00:28:41.932 --> 00:28:44.901
...aside from wait for an early demise...

00:28:45.802 --> 00:28:48.532
...and ask really dumb questions?

00:28:49.640 --> 00:28:53.804
Actually I brought you up here to tell you
something very important.

00:28:54.444 --> 00:28:56.207
Grover.

00:28:56.580 --> 00:28:57.911
Grover?

00:28:58.081 --> 00:28:59.776
It's my nickname.

00:28:59.950 --> 00:29:01.417
I always loved Grover as a kid.

00:29:01.585 --> 00:29:04.486
I know for most kids it's all
Winnie the Pooh or Hello Kitty...

00:29:04.655 --> 00:29:07.590
...or occasionally Strawberry Shortcake...

00:29:07.758 --> 00:29:11.319
...but for me life was about
a little blue Muppet named Grover.

00:29:11.495 --> 00:29:14.430
Well Grover was a very
underrated Muppet.

00:29:15.666 --> 00:29:20.103
Colin and Bright used to torment me
by stealing my Grover doll and hiding him.

00:29:20.270 --> 00:29:24.172
And then one day Colin refused to give me
the doll back unless I kissed him first.

00:29:24.341 --> 00:29:26.332
Colin that is not Grover who...

00:29:26.510 --> 00:29:29.172
...I had kissed many many times.

00:29:29.346 --> 00:29:32.577
So I closed my eyes Colin closed his.

00:29:32.749 --> 00:29:35.183
We both leaned forward.

00:29:35.986 --> 00:29:37.647
And I kicked him right in the nuts.

00:29:37.821 --> 00:29:40.654
Colin that is not Grover
who didn't have nuts.

00:29:40.824 --> 00:29:42.724
At least none that I was aware of.

00:29:42.893 --> 00:29:46.659
Anyway Colin screamed
and doubled over.

00:29:46.830 --> 00:29:50.231
My parents raced into the room
and when they asked what happened...

00:29:50.400 --> 00:29:52.595
...Colin wouldn't tell them.

00:29:53.270 --> 00:29:55.898
All he would say was that Grover did it.

00:29:56.773 --> 00:29:58.900
And somehow suddenly I had...

00:29:59.076 --> 00:30:01.271
...developed my first crush.

00:30:03.046 --> 00:30:04.980
On Colin that is...

00:30:05.749 --> 00:30:07.444
...not Grover.

00:30:11.154 --> 00:30:15.215
Look I know we haven't talked
about this since that trip to Denver so...

00:30:17.294 --> 00:30:19.762
You want me to ask my dad to help Colin.

00:30:19.930 --> 00:30:22.558
If you could just talk to him.

00:30:22.733 --> 00:30:25.361
I mean I know there's probably
nothing he can do but...

00:30:25.535 --> 00:30:29.904
Yeah. Sure Amy. I'll ask him. No problem.

00:30:30.974 --> 00:30:32.942
Thank you.

00:30:37.314 --> 00:30:39.748
Dr. Brown! Care to try for a wish?

00:30:40.183 --> 00:30:42.981
- Anything for my premier patient.
- Such a doll doctor!

00:30:43.153 --> 00:30:45.144
All you do is drop a quarter in the tank.

00:30:45.322 --> 00:30:47.790
If it lands in those shot glasses
you get your wish.

00:30:47.991 --> 00:30:51.392
It costs 50 cents not counting
the 25 cents in the tank of course.

00:30:51.561 --> 00:30:54.462
All the money goes to benefit
the girls dance troupe I teach...

00:30:54.731 --> 00:30:59.395
...The Everwood Swans.
We have a recital coming up this fall.

00:31:17.220 --> 00:31:18.949
You know what's funny?

00:31:19.122 --> 00:31:22.182
I didn't get the coin in the glass
but I still got my wish.

00:31:22.359 --> 00:31:23.621
You're lucky that way.

00:31:25.962 --> 00:31:27.987
Aren't you gonna tell me why I'm here?

00:31:28.465 --> 00:31:30.729
I wanted to see you...

00:31:31.067 --> 00:31:34.161
...know that you're more
than just a memory...

00:31:34.838 --> 00:31:36.806
...and tell you that I kept my promise.

00:31:37.574 --> 00:31:39.599
You didn't keep yours.

00:31:40.444 --> 00:31:42.878
You promised you'd be here...

00:31:43.079 --> 00:31:44.740
...in Everwood...

00:31:45.215 --> 00:31:46.580
...but you're not.

00:31:48.018 --> 00:31:50.486
I've got bad news for you Andy
you're gonna be fine.

00:31:50.654 --> 00:31:51.882
"Fine" is not great.

00:31:52.055 --> 00:31:55.047
You've had enough of "great."
It isn't all it's cracked up to be.

00:31:56.960 --> 00:31:59.053
Fine is real.

00:32:01.832 --> 00:32:03.459
Now come on...

00:32:03.633 --> 00:32:04.930
...say it.

00:32:06.703 --> 00:32:08.671
Say what?

00:32:08.839 --> 00:32:10.864
Goodbye.

00:32:12.342 --> 00:32:14.708
That's why you wanted
to see me isn't it?

00:32:14.878 --> 00:32:16.505
You wanted to say goodbye.

00:32:16.680 --> 00:32:21.049
No! No not to you. Just to...

00:32:21.751 --> 00:32:23.412
To this.

00:32:23.587 --> 00:32:25.418
I understand.

00:32:25.589 --> 00:32:27.580
You do?

00:32:27.757 --> 00:32:29.918
Besides I was never the reason.

00:32:31.094 --> 00:32:34.188
- I don't get it.
- He was Andy.

00:32:35.165 --> 00:32:38.100
You came here so you could know him.

00:32:38.602 --> 00:32:40.467
Know who?

00:33:04.694 --> 00:33:06.889
Let's go home Dad.

00:33:30.086 --> 00:33:31.917
So...

00:33:32.489 --> 00:33:34.582
...what did everyone think of the festival?

00:33:35.759 --> 00:33:39.195
- No it's not funny.
- It's a little funny.

00:33:46.202 --> 00:33:48.693
- What's this?
- It's a note from school.

00:33:48.872 --> 00:33:50.305
I'm in big trouble.

00:33:52.676 --> 00:33:54.769
See you inside!

00:33:56.012 --> 00:33:58.537
She's crafty that one.

00:34:03.453 --> 00:34:07.116
I see her too sometimes.

00:34:07.891 --> 00:34:13.659
Mom I mean. Not like you do.
I don't talk to her or anything.

00:34:14.064 --> 00:34:15.554
More like...

00:34:15.732 --> 00:34:17.700
...I feel her...

00:34:18.335 --> 00:34:19.996
...with us.

00:34:20.470 --> 00:34:22.028
When we're all having dinner...

00:34:22.739 --> 00:34:26.675
...or when there's a song playing
on the radio she used to like.

00:34:27.077 --> 00:34:29.841
I just know she's there.

00:34:34.784 --> 00:34:38.185
Ephram I wish I could tell you
everything's going to be okay.

00:34:38.622 --> 00:34:41.955
I know that's what I'm supposed
to say but the truth is...

00:34:42.125 --> 00:34:44.685
...I don't know what's going
to happen to us.

00:34:45.261 --> 00:34:48.992
What I do know is that
all we have now is each other.

00:34:50.300 --> 00:34:53.133
I need your help raising your sister.

00:34:53.803 --> 00:34:56.135
I can't do it alone.

00:34:57.007 --> 00:34:59.339
She gets us.

00:35:33.176 --> 00:35:35.576
- Morning doctor.
- Good morning.

00:35:37.247 --> 00:35:38.475
What's the matter?

00:35:38.948 --> 00:35:41.815
Didn't have time for your usual
bowl of sarcasm this morning?

00:35:41.985 --> 00:35:45.716
I wanted to thank you for giving my son
and daughter a ride the other night.

00:35:46.156 --> 00:35:47.589
That was very kind of you.

00:35:47.757 --> 00:35:49.349
You're welcome.

00:35:49.793 --> 00:35:52.728
Since you seem hell-bent
on becoming a permanent fixture here...

00:35:52.896 --> 00:35:54.761
...I should give you a piece of advice.

00:35:55.198 --> 00:35:56.631
And that is?

00:35:57.200 --> 00:35:59.191
When I first joined my father's practice...

00:35:59.369 --> 00:36:04.204
...I too went out of my way to be
available to all people at all times.

00:36:04.374 --> 00:36:07.138
I realized that exhausting myself
was no good for anyone...

00:36:07.310 --> 00:36:10.245
...least of all for my family
who needed me the most.

00:36:11.014 --> 00:36:14.347
Being a small-town physician
is a marathon doctor not a sprint.

00:36:15.051 --> 00:36:17.485
And if one of us is going
to win this race...

00:36:17.654 --> 00:36:20.214
...you are going to have to stay in it.

00:36:22.225 --> 00:36:23.920
And behold the people...

00:36:25.028 --> 00:36:28.361
...who had every attribute of dogs...

00:36:28.932 --> 00:36:31.162
...except loyalty.

00:36:31.701 --> 00:36:33.066
Go on everyone.

00:36:33.236 --> 00:36:35.864
- Inside.
- Thank you doctor.

00:36:36.039 --> 00:36:37.734
Welcome back.

00:36:38.975 --> 00:36:41.773
All is forgiven.

00:36:50.687 --> 00:36:52.279
You hear that?

00:36:52.455 --> 00:36:54.548
That was the sound of a pin dropping.

00:36:54.724 --> 00:36:57.488
After what happened
I'm surprised you're still here Edna.

00:36:58.361 --> 00:37:00.420
You're paying me.

00:37:02.132 --> 00:37:04.396
We're in this foxhole together <i>compadre</i>.

00:37:04.768 --> 00:37:06.531
Don't worry about everyone else.

00:37:06.703 --> 00:37:08.398
They'll come around. They always do.

00:37:08.571 --> 00:37:12.439
It's sort of the nature of this place.
You're up one day you're down the next.

00:37:12.609 --> 00:37:16.045
In the meantime we have
some excellent periodicals.

00:37:23.686 --> 00:37:26.246
- Morning doctor.
- Mrs. Dudley what a nice surprise.

00:37:26.422 --> 00:37:28.390
- How are you?
- Just fine thank you.

00:37:29.292 --> 00:37:33.922
I wanted to stop by and take the
opportunity to say thank you again.

00:37:34.097 --> 00:37:36.531
Well that's quite a long way just to...

00:37:38.468 --> 00:37:40.163
How did you get here?

00:37:40.336 --> 00:37:43.328
I heard about what happened yesterday...

00:37:43.506 --> 00:37:46.304
...and I wanted to tell you
that my family...

00:37:46.476 --> 00:37:49.138
Well like a lot of other
families around here...

00:37:49.312 --> 00:37:53.510
...we don't have much
but now we have a doctor.

00:37:55.518 --> 00:37:58.453
I know it was a tragedy
that brought you here sir.

00:37:58.621 --> 00:38:00.521
For that I am sorry.

00:38:00.690 --> 00:38:03.454
But I'm not sorry that you came.

00:38:05.995 --> 00:38:08.395
Neither am I Mrs. Dudley.

00:38:11.134 --> 00:38:13.102
You take care now.

00:38:15.138 --> 00:38:17.265
Well at least offer her a ride home.

00:38:20.276 --> 00:38:22.836
Mrs. Dudley!

00:38:26.216 --> 00:38:28.548
- How's it going there ham?
- Ham?

00:38:28.718 --> 00:38:31.949
- It's your new nickname. Welcome to it.
- My nickname's a deli item.

00:38:32.121 --> 00:38:36.421
See that's what everyone will think
but we'll know it's really short for this.

00:38:37.760 --> 00:38:40.126
See? You look just like Hamlet.

00:38:42.031 --> 00:38:43.396
That does not look like me.

00:38:43.566 --> 00:38:47.969
No no you can't deny it.
Everwood finally has its own dark prince.

00:38:49.172 --> 00:38:51.037
You want to grab some lunch?

00:38:52.642 --> 00:38:54.974
Before we get lunch we should talk.

00:38:56.746 --> 00:38:58.680
You asked your father didn't you?

00:39:03.453 --> 00:39:04.977
He said no.

00:39:08.191 --> 00:39:10.250
I mean you can't really begrudge the guy.

00:39:10.426 --> 00:39:13.918
He's trying to get out of the brain business
start a new life.

00:39:16.299 --> 00:39:18.494
I don't know what I was thinking.

00:39:18.668 --> 00:39:20.795
I'm sorry. It was silly for me to ask.

00:39:21.204 --> 00:39:23.138
I'm sorry Amy.

00:39:27.644 --> 00:39:30.135
You still want to get lunch?

00:39:31.147 --> 00:39:33.308
I think I'm just gonna hang here a while...

00:39:33.783 --> 00:39:36.877
...and look over some notes before class.

00:40:00.009 --> 00:40:02.239
Your daughter has a mind
of her own Dr. Brown.

00:40:02.412 --> 00:40:06.610
She repeatedly interrupts my lessons
with questions that make very little sense.

00:40:06.783 --> 00:40:09.616
This in addition to her
inappropriate apparel...

00:40:09.786 --> 00:40:12.118
I've never been to
a parent-teacher thingy.

00:40:12.288 --> 00:40:13.846
Am I allowed to speak?

00:40:14.023 --> 00:40:15.888
You have to raise your hand.

00:40:16.059 --> 00:40:19.654
- Excuse me Dr. Brown!
- I'm sorry. Just out of curiosity Miss Violet.

00:40:19.829 --> 00:40:21.524
Why do the boys sit in the front?

00:40:22.699 --> 00:40:26.100
Very simple. Boys are rowdier.

00:40:26.302 --> 00:40:29.100
- Rowdier?
- They cause more of a fuss.

00:40:29.272 --> 00:40:32.799
By having them sit in the front
I can monitor their behavior more closely.

00:40:33.009 --> 00:40:36.672
You believe girls are genetically less rowdy
so you relegate them to the back?

00:40:36.879 --> 00:40:39.347
- The term "relegate" is...
- Entirely appropriate.

00:40:39.615 --> 00:40:43.016
As for Delia having a mind of her own
whose mind is she supposed to have?

00:40:43.186 --> 00:40:46.952
- I think you misunderstood my point.
- No I don't think that I did.

00:40:47.724 --> 00:40:50.852
Delia perhaps you should step outside
while your father and l...

00:40:51.027 --> 00:40:54.758
No no. She was here for the bad part.
I want her to hear what I'm about to say.

00:40:55.865 --> 00:41:00.529
My daughter has been through a traumatic
year and come through it remarkably well.

00:41:00.903 --> 00:41:03.736
I'd like to take more credit for that
but I can't.

00:41:03.906 --> 00:41:06.739
She's the product of a mother
who taught her about strength...

00:41:06.909 --> 00:41:09.469
...courage and independence
from an early age.

00:41:09.645 --> 00:41:12.876
My job is to make sure she doesn't
forget those lessons.

00:41:13.049 --> 00:41:16.917
She will sit wherever you tell her to sit
but as long as she's polite about it...

00:41:17.086 --> 00:41:19.077
...she can ask all the questions she wants.

00:41:19.255 --> 00:41:23.589
And I'd get used to those baseball caps.
As for you and me...

00:41:23.926 --> 00:41:26.827
...you can keep calling me in here
but next time...

00:41:26.996 --> 00:41:32.059
...my daughter better have done something
wrong or you'll have one rowdy father.

00:41:32.468 --> 00:41:36.564
- This meeting is over doctor!
- Yes it certainly is.

00:41:37.206 --> 00:41:38.867
Come on Delia.

00:41:39.242 --> 00:41:40.937
See you tomorrow Miss Violet.

00:41:49.285 --> 00:41:52.413
- Where have you two been?
- You want to tell him or should I?

00:41:52.588 --> 00:41:53.953
We went horse shopping.

00:41:54.123 --> 00:41:56.990
There's a ranch just off the highway
that breeds horses.

00:41:57.160 --> 00:41:59.856
Dad took me there.
We just looked though.

00:42:00.029 --> 00:42:02.554
- Finally making good on that bribe?
- You cooked dinner?

00:42:02.732 --> 00:42:05.132
We should have meat-loaf-flavored
meat loaf for once.

00:42:05.301 --> 00:42:06.700
How's the hand doing?

00:42:09.539 --> 00:42:13.407
Tell you what I'll stay away from recipes
that involve three or more ingredients...

00:42:13.576 --> 00:42:16.670
...you stay away from the first-aid kit.
- It's a deal.

00:42:16.846 --> 00:42:20.612
Now go on. Sit down. Dinner's ready.

00:42:27.657 --> 00:42:31.821
<i>The first fall thaw that Andy Brown</i>
<i>and his children ever knew...</i>

00:42:31.994 --> 00:42:34.292
<i>... passed through Everwood</i>
<i>later that night...</i>

00:42:34.464 --> 00:42:38.423
<i>... taking with it our last bit</i>
<i>of warm autumn air...</i>

00:42:38.601 --> 00:42:41.297
...<i>but not our warmth of spirit.</i>

00:42:41.471 --> 00:42:43.735
<i>That was in the people of Everwood...</i>

00:42:43.906 --> 00:42:45.703
<i>... and in our hearts...</i>

00:42:45.875 --> 00:42:48.708
<i>... some broken, some mending...</i>

00:42:48.878 --> 00:42:53.110
<i>... and some, for the moment, complete.</i>

00:43:47.170 --> 00:43:49.161
[ENGLISH]
